- op: update  # ebcf
  at: '2026-10-26T00:28:42Z'  # ebcf
  by: agent  # ebcf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ebcf
  clock: 4  # ebcf
  nonce: ebcf  # ebcf
  set:  # ebcf
    description: "Proposed 2026-10-25 from a review of all 19 recorded Fundamental Concept Audits; filed on the owner's request as the input for the next audit when the cadence comes due (54 non-tracker commits since audit #19 at 2026-10-25, threshold 72).\n\nFINDING. The audits are built to find one name carrying two meanings (the four leakage tests), and those often came back clean (#3 layering, #9 identity axis, #10 type kinds, #16 ten of twelve values). The defect that recurred across them was different and was always found in passing: a field, meta key, knob or function that NOTHING READS, or a documented claim nothing enforces. Instances: origin_run_signature, run_signature and linker pass_version (#4); DataModel.kind (#5; deletion ruled 2026-10-25, WI-tikan); requires_symbols and validate_pass_dependencies (#6; the latter deleted 2026-10-25, PR #1864); TaintSink.trust_level (#3 kept it as an extension point, #15 found it a promised control with no effect); directness and analysis_tiers (#8); shape_id (#9); 34 unregistered Edge.meta keys (#13); receiver_type_hint unread at the io_boundary/taint seam (#14, WI-monul still open); AnalysisRun.skipped_passes and limits.skipped_languages (#17). LIVE.md rule 7: an instrument with no reader is the same defect. Nobody has swept for it directly.\n\nSCOPE (the inventory, with a production-reader count for each): every field on the dataclasses in ir.py, datamodels.py and io_boundary.py (and TaintSource / TaintSink / TaintFlowFinding in taint.py); every registered meta key in axis_meta_keys.py (MetaKeySpec entries) and every meta key actually emitted; every config knob (SupplyChainConfig, .hypergumbo.toml keys, config.toml keys, CLI flags, environment variables read); every public module-level function in packages/*/src with no production caller (scripts/check-test-only-reachability already lists the test-only ones -- start from its baseline).\nMETHOD. Find readers with an AST walk across all five Step-4.5 emit/read shapes, never grep alone: audit #16's grep missed 126 of 140 emit sites written in dict-literal form, and #17's grep called two live values dead. A serialised field counts as read only if something consumes the serialised output (a CLI view, a documented JSON contract, a test that pins a consumer), not merely because to_dict() writes it -- #5 found DataModel.to_dict() itself never called. Measure across configurations, not only defaults (#17 missed a third outcome behind HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1).\nVERDICTS per item: DELETE (no reader and none intended), WIRE (a reader is needed and missing -- name it), DECLARE EXTERNAL (deliberately written for an outside consumer; say which, in the field's docstring, as #9 did for run_signature), or KEEP WITH A TRIGGER THAT CAN FIRE. A trigger of the form 'when a consumer appears' cannot fire on a field nothing reads, so it is not accepted (#5's DataModelKind triggers and INV-hujog's original trigger were both unfireable). Also re-check every existing keep-with-trigger verdict from the 19 audits for whether its trigger can fire at all.\nDELIVERABLE: the per-item table (docs/audits/ or the lab notebook per docs/audits/README.md scope), filed items for each DELETE/WIRE verdict, and the audit recorded with scripts/concept-audit-record. Every action in the write-up names a tracker id (audit #8's F1 was listed only as an action and was lost for three months). Related: the axiom-falsification item filed beside this one; WI-monul; WI-tikan; WI-mujug; WI-punod.\n\nSCOPE WIDENED 2026-10-25 (owner request, from a review of how this sweep bears on the 2026-10-21 concept-audit rows and the 10-25 premise-check rows). Four additions to METHOD/SCOPE, and three named items whose decision this sweep now owns.\n\nA. THE INVERSE SHAPE: a READER WITH NO PRODUCER. A consumer keyed to a value, key or shape nothing emits is the same defect from the other side (LIVE rule 7). Count producers for every read, as well as readers for every write. Instances: INV-fuhin (supply_chain_summary reads directness on dependency declarations; nothing stamps it there, and the registry text and spec say it does); WI-sorav's channel_kind example 'message_queue' (declared; producers emit queue).\n\nB. CATALOGUE AND OVERLAY FILE KEYS ARE KNOBS. Add every key the YAML loaders accept (io_primitives / io_primitives.d overlays, taint_sources.d / --taint-sources, taint_sinks / --taint-sinks, claims files) to the knob inventory, with a reader for each. An accepted key that nothing reads is a write-only knob. Instance: WI-rinaz (a user taint-source file's attributes: key is reported loaded and contributes nothing).\n\nC. CLASSIFY EACH READER, NOT ONLY COUNT IT: display / presence check / branch on the value (ADR-0058's distinction). This is what checks a 'free-text -- consumers never branch' declaration: ADR-0058 leaves its remaining free-text declarations unswept, and WI-fuzat's DefaultOverlay.provenance ('never parsed', compared as an enum by declares_community) is a second one shown false. Two shapes a per-field count misses, so record them per QUESTION, not per field: (i) read by some consumers but not by the one that decides the question (WI-monul: receiver_type_hint has linker and owner_ancestry readers, none in io_boundary/taint); (ii) written to an object that is then discarded (WI-gidid: run.warnings appended on a run collect_analyzer_result drops).\n\nD. CONSUMER-SIDE SUBSETS OF A REGISTERED VOCABULARY. A hand-written set or partition of a declared vocabulary drifts when the vocabulary grows; the registry linter, the axis rule and a reader count all pass it. Inventory every such subset with the vocabulary it partitions and whether every value is placed in or out. Instances: receiver_blind_magnets._RECEIVER_MARKERS lacks declared_type / self / bare / generic (WI-sibup, a P2 wrong edge); slice _CONTAINER_KINDS and type_like_kind_names (WI-totam); prerequisite_absent_clauses' != no_candidate_files proxy and ROUTINE_SILENCE_REASONS, which disagree (WI-punod); the empty-zone gate's two zones (WI-sojok); CHOICE_SHAPED_SOURCE_NAMES (WI-zakil part 3). Deliverable for D: a proposed gate requiring each subset to be a declared, complete partition (red when a value is added unplaced), filed as its own item; the per-instance fixes stay on their items and do not wait for this sweep.\n\nNAMED ITEMS THIS SWEEP DECIDES (verdict from DELETE / WIRE / DECLARE EXTERNAL / KEEP WITH A FIREABLE TRIGGER):\n- WI-fomif: bakeoff-deep's claims_confirmed / claim_verdict_pct -- the item records no reader. Decide DELETE vs WIRE (name the reader) before anyone fixes the count; fixing a number nobody reads is rule 7.\n- The keep-with-trigger on the generic Edge.meta keys call_type and method (concept audit 2026-10-21, WI-sorav; the decision deferred to WI-kuhoh): 're-audit on their first reader' is the unfireable trigger form this sweep refuses. Replace it with a fireable verdict; WI-kuhoh's other halves (keys written on both Symbol.meta and Edge.meta) take this sweep's registered-vs-emitted table as their data.\n- WI-mujug: meta['receiver'] (11 values, 2 readers at its 2026-10-25 re-check) and meta['resolution_quality'] -- this sweep's meta-key inventory with reader classification (C) and subset check (D) is the audit WI-mujug asks for; decide both keys here."  # ebcf
